      "role": "rules",
      "chars": 1563,
      "text": "SCENE CONVENTIONS\n- Units are meters, kilograms and seconds in a right-handed, Z-up world frame. The floor top surface is at z = 0.\n- quaternion_wxyz is an active rotation from the object's local frame to the world frame, ordered [w, x, y, z], unit length. A pure yaw of theta radians about +Z is [cos(theta/2), 0, 0, sin(theta/2)]; yawing an object by delta multiplies its current quaternion on the left by that yaw quaternion.\n- geometry.aabb_local_min/max is the object's bounding box in its own frame (it rotates with the object). geometry.aabb_world_min/max is the same box in world coordinates at the CURRENT pose; recompute it yourself if you rotate the object.\n- geometry.support_anchor_local is the lowest point of the object in its local frame. An unrotated (or yaw-only rotated) object resting on a horizontal support of height h has position z = h - support_anchor_local[2]. Objects with different heights therefore need different z values at the same support.\n- geometry.semantic_front_axis_local is the object's forward direction in its local frame (null for objects without a front). The object faces a target when its rotated front axis points at the target in the XY plane.\n- support_patches lists horizontal support surfaces (floor top, table top) with their world height and extent (bounds_local_m are in the parent's frame; add the parent's position).\n- cameras describe the attached images: \"front\" is a room overview and \"tabletop\" a close-up of the table. Use the images to identify objects by color; the scene JSON holds the exact numbers."
