      "text": "HOW THE ANSWER IS CHECKED (deterministic checks in the PhysX simulator)\n- \"closer to X\": the XY center distance between the object and X must shrink by at least 0.20 m.\n- \"face X\", \"turn toward X\": the angle between the object's rotated front axis and the XY direction from the object to X must be at most 15 degrees.\n- \"swap places\", \"exchange locations\": each object's XY center must land within 0.035 m of the other object's original XY center. Each object keeps its own z and its own orientation unless told otherwise (two objects can have different heights).\n- \"against the wall with a small clear gap\": the object's world bounding box must end 0.025 to 0.25 m from the wall plane (room_bounds_m).\n- \"beside one another with space between\": the horizontal gap between the two bounding boxes must be 0.025 to 0.18 m, and each object must rest on the table with at least 80% of its footprint over the table top.\n- \"between A and B\": the object's XY center must project onto the segment from A's center to B's center, at most 0.09 m from that line, resting on the table.\n- \"keep in place\" / \"leave orientation unchanged\": do not emit that field (null); every object you were not asked to move must keep its exact original pose, so do not include it.\n- Physical screens after the edit: no interpenetration deeper than 3 mm; everything inside room_bounds_m; moved furniture upright (tilt at most 10 degrees); after one second of simulated settling no object may have moved more than 15 mm, rotated more than 3 degrees, or still be moving. So place each moved object exactly on its support (z from support_anchor_local), clear of every other object's bounding box, and with a plausible clearance (a chair \"close to\" a table should not overlap the table top)."
